# Environments
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Training artifacts and datasets — regenerable, and far too large for git
# (runs/ is 232 MB, synthetic_dataset/ is 143 MB)
runs/
synthetic_dataset/
wandb/
*.log

# Model weights. The author tracks the ONNX baseline; these are local extras.
yolo11n.pt
*.pt
*.onnx.bak
assets/models/vision/hand_landmarker.task
# Same deal, fetched by tools/face_landmarker README note rather than tracked:
#   curl -o assets/models/vision/face_landmarker.task \
#     https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task
assets/models/vision/face_landmarker.task

# Sliced print files. The .step sources are the useful artifact and are tracked;
# .gcode.3mf is slicer output specific to one printer and profile, and the set
# runs to tens of megabytes.
*.gcode.3mf

# Scratch images from ad-hoc debugging
gt.png
rl_path_flow.png
vision_path_flow.png

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Secrets — none are present today, keep it that way
.env
.env.*
*.key

# RL training output — PPO checkpoints, ~210 MB of .zip model snapshots across
# three runs. The trained policy that the robot actually uses is tracked under
# assets/models/; these are the intermediate steps that produced it.
results/

# Stereo calibration capture set — 55 MB of raw checkerboard JPEGs. The derived
# calibration (stereo_params.pickle et al) is tracked; the captures are not, and
# they are specific to one camera mount.
data/

# MuJoCo scratch
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
exploration/__pycache__/
exploration/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private working notes. The public repo carries README.md (the build writeup)
# and UPSTREAM_README.md, and nothing else in prose form; these are personal
# build logs, forward-looking plans, and supplier details. Code comments were
# rewritten to be self-contained so nothing public depends on them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LESSONS_LEARNED.md
CLOSED_LOOP_DEBUG.md
HARDWARE_DAY.md
HARDWARE_PROCUREMENT.md
HARDWARE_LEROBOT_SETUP.md
ROADMAP.md
NEXT_PHASE_EXPLORATION.md
PRINTING.md
PRINT_CHECKLIST.md
MEMORY.md
exploration/MOTION_SPACE_NOTES.md

# Measurement artifacts from the characterisation series. The tools that produce
# them are tracked and self-documenting; the raw CSV/PNG output is run-specific
# and its explanatory README is a private note, so the data would ship
# uninterpretable.
diagnostics/

# Next-phase design exploration — scratch tooling for a future form factor,
# not part of this build.
exploration/

# Perception and gesture recordings written by the exploration tools
# (face_probe --csv, puppet's gesture takes). Same reasoning as diagnostics/:
# the tools are tracked and self-describing, the takes are session-specific and
# contain footage-derived data about whoever happened to be in front of the
# cameras, which is not something to publish by default.
out/

# Ad-hoc plots dumped at the repo root. Every one is a command away from being
# remade from the CSVs or a recording, and they go stale the moment a table is
# edited -- the tables and the tools are tracked, their output is not.
# Scoped to the root ON PURPOSE: a bare *.png would also silence media/ and
# assets/, where 35 tracked images live, including every figure the README
# writeup depends on. Adding a new one would then fail silently.
/*.png
/*.numbers
